1
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoes go flying too.

3
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:32,920
Will you give me a choking hold, I wonder?

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,140
They laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I've left my energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
Katsushika, a sigh, a yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed hat's flask,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
the sun sets toward the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,610 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end just like this too,
won't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,020
Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness is lost.

12
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,700
Bonus: The Day the Chimney Disappeared

13
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:38,500
Stay back!

14
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:41,000
Ryotsu!

15
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:43,120
Ryo-chan! Be careful!

16
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:44,240
Senpai!

17
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:48,520
Stay back!
No matter who comes, I'm not coming down!

18
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:56,180
I'm not coming down, so don't bother.

19
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:59,260
If you don't want to come down,
you don't have to.

20
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:02,020
But at least tell us why.

21
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,220
Heave-ho, here we go!

22
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,300
Tell me, Jumpei.

23
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,020
What on earth happened?

24
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:14,240
Mom broke her promise, that's what.

25
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:15,700
Promise?

26
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:17,920
The movie, Pekomon.

27
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:20,660
If we don't go today, it'll be over!

28
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:24,320
I see. So that's why you're
on strike atop the chimney.

29
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:26,940
Mom's always like this.

30
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:29,108
Saying she has something
came up or whatever,

31
00:02:29,158 --> 00:02:32,060
she thinks it's fine to
break a promise to me.

32
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,560
That's so unfair! We promised!

33
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:43,348
It's somehow nostalgic, isn't it.

34
00:02:43,398 --> 00:02:46,060
Looking out over the town
from atop a chimney like this.

35
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:50,780
You've climbed a chimney too, Ryo-san?

36
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:54,280
Back then there were no tall buildings,

37
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:56,480
and even that was bluer, too.

38
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:02,120
The one I climbed was called the Senju Ghost Chimney,
you see.

39
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,960
It was even taller than this one.

40
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,380
Ghost Chimney.

41
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:10,660
That's right, it was the chimney of a thermal
power plant said to be the largest in Japan.

42
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:15,440
Back then there were few buildings, so you
could see it from anywhere in the old downtown.

43
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:18,600
Those four huge chimneys, you see,

44
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:22,040
look like a different number depending
on which direction you view them from.

45
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:24,220
From the Sumida River, there are three.

46
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:26,620
From Senju Ōhashi, there are two, they say.

47
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:28,680
That's why they were
called the Ghost Chimneys.

48
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:29,700
Yeah.

49
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:33,400
So we'd often use the number
of visible chimneys as a code.

50
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:35,620
Like, "Let's meet where
you can see just one."

51
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:40,440
Yeah, that's right.

52
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:42,980
I could've sworn we agreed on one, though.

53
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:46,080
What are Jumpei and Chinkitsu doing?

54
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:55,240
Oh no, what should I do?

55
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:58,260
Did the chain come off?

56
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:02,800
Let me have a look, I'll fix it for you.

57
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:04,980
Thank you.

58
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:08,500
For this, if you just do this here,

59
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:15,400
Wow, a secret base That's amazing!

60
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:19,100
There, done.

61
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:22,200
You're really handy, aren't you?

62
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:25,180
This is a piece of cake for me.

63
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:26,780
Oh my.

64
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:30,560
Well then, Densuke-san.

65
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:31,400
Yeah.

66
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:41,620
Thanks, you really saved me.

67
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:45,720
Well then,

68
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:52,540
Kankichi!

69
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:55,640
Sorry I'm late.

70
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:58,060
Y-yeah.

71
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:01,800
Sorry, sorry,
I got held up collecting all this stuff.

72
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:06,760
Snakes?
You're gonna be scared stiff, for sure.

73
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:10,260
Thanks to Mr. Kuruma getting hit by
a truck and ending up in the hospital,

74
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:11,680
we've got more fun to look forward to

75
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,280
Well, the start is what
matters most in everything.

76
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,480
First, we'll drop water
on them with a bucket,

77
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:20,860
and now I can't wait for tomorrow!

78
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:31,680
We've got three problem kids, you know. Jumpei,
Chinkitsu, and Kankichi, a trio of three idiots.

79
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:37,100
Well, it's only until our homeroom teacher, Mr. Kuruma,
gets out of the hospital, so please just go along without deciding anything.

80
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:38,060
Yes.

81
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,240
Yay, it was a huge success!

82
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:46,720
Yay, yay!

83
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:54,180
H-hey, who's there?

84
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:55,960
Whoever did such a terrible thing,

85
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:58,540
Kankichi, it's you again, isn't it?

86
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:00,980
You idiot! Money can't buy which one...

87
00:06:01,430 --> 00:06:02,360
Vice-Principal!

88
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:05,360
I'm fine, really.

89
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:08,180
Well, but this guy...

90
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:11,200
It's fine, he's my student.

91
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:14,500
Yesterday's

92
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:21,660
Nice to meet you.

93
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:27,380
I'll be the homeroom teacher for Class
4-3 until Kuruma-sensei leaves the hospital.

94
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:28,900
I'm Yoko Saeki.

95
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:31,280
Nice to meet you all.

96
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:33,720
Please take care of me.

97
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:52,080
Kankichi, let's stop with the snake stuff.

98
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:55,500
Yeah, I never expected
a female teacher, either.

99
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:58,640
No, a man follows through
on what he's decided.

100
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:19,000
On second thought, forget the snake.

101
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:30,540
There, there, I'll let you go, you hear?

102
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:32,460
Is there or isn't there?

103
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:34,360
Kankichi!

104
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,440
Uh-oh.

105
00:07:36,780 --> 00:07:38,300
What are you doing up this late at night?

106
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,840
Hey, stop right there!

107
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:46,860
I don't know!

108
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:51,260
Then who on earth broke the championship
cup from the principal's office?

109
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:52,940
I didn't do it, I'm telling you!

110
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:54,140
Don't lie!

111
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:57,280
I saw you sneaking into
this classroom last night.

112
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:59,140
I saw it with my own eyes.

113
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:00,180
That was...

114
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:02,880
Is that so?

115
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:06,900
So you all suspect me

116
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:07,620
Kankichi-kun

117
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:11,300
Look me in the eye and tell the truth.

118
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:14,260
It wasn't me. I'm not lying.

119
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:20,540
Don't be fooled, Teacher Saeki.

120
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:23,700
This boy is the biggest
troublemaker in the school.

121
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:27,040
I said it's not me. You all know that too.

122
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:31,000
We won this cup at the district
tournament because of my performance.

123
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,280
So why would I be the one to break it?

124
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,460
Damn it, forget it then.

125
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:42,200
Kankichi

126
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:49,240
Why, why? You're all idiots!

127
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:05,100
Damn it, everyone, you idiots!

128
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:08,800
You too, teacher, you idiot!

129
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:10,520
Kankichi-kun!

130
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:12,840
Kankichi-kun!

131
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:16,660
So you were up here after all.

132
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:19,680
What, you're suspecting me too,
aren't you, teacher?

133
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,040
That's not true.

134
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:26,800
Kankichi-kun,
you fixed my bicycle chain, didn't you?

135
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:31,260
Well, that's...
but that has nothing to do with it!

136
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,340
I'm the one who dumped
the bucket of water, too!

137
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,340
Hey, Kankichi-kun.

138
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:37,880
From there, how many chimneys can you see?

139
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,680
It's obviously just one.

140
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:43,340
Yeah.

141
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:47,400
It does look like one, that's for sure.

142
00:09:47,900 --> 00:09:50,940
But that chimney actually has four.

143
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:54,720
Depending on the angle you look from,
it can look like one,

144
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:57,140
or two, or three.

145
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,400
That's why it's called
the Ghost Chimney, right?

146
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:01,740
I know that already.

147
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:05,180
Hey, Kankichi,
don't you think people are like that too?

148
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:10,720
Depending on the angle you look from,
one person shows many different sides.

149
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,820
Sometimes they're a troublemaker,
sometimes they're considerate.

150
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:18,700
But I don't think a person's
essential nature ever really changes.

151
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:19,900
Essential nature?

152
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:22,200
I guess you could call it their true self.

153
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:27,280
For you, Kankichi, I think it's the kindness
you showed when you fixed that chain.

154
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,500
So let's keep our heads high and
have the courage to stand tall.

155
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:34,120
I believe you didn't do it, Kankichi.

156
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:47,480
Is that true?

157
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,120
Yeah.

158
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:50,900
The Class 2 guys, after school yesterday,

159
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,680
apparently broke it by
hitting it with a dodgeball.

160
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:55,300
We finally found the girl who saw it happen.

161
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:57,040
It was Naohito and Kazuya.

162
00:10:57,540 --> 00:10:58,100
Thanks, guys.

163
00:10:58,100 --> 00:10:59,800
Tonpe, Chinkitsu.

164
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:02,680
You two really are my bosom buddies.

165
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:03,440
Damn it.

166
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:06,760
Knock it off,
or I'll beat the crap out of you.

167
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:08,600
No, Kankichi-kun.

168
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,440
You can't resort to
violence over everything.

169
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:14,440
Yes, Sensei.

170
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:18,640
Why did Kankichi get caught up in this?

171
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:19,420
Well...

172
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,700
They're taking their time coming down,
aren't they?

173
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:42,900
Looks like they're deep in conversation.

174
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:44,980
Ever since then,

175
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:48,460
she comes in first thing in the morning
and polishes the blackboard until it shines,

176
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:51,640
and even puts flowers on the teacher's desk.

177
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:55,800
When it's time for a home visit,
she's in a complete panic.

178
00:11:57,620 --> 00:11:59,720
Trouble, trouble, trouble!

179
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:03,900
Kinjiro,
don't go studying in a place like this!

180
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:07,265
Dad, stop sleeping over there.

181
00:12:07,315 --> 00:12:10,400
The teacher's almost here,
so everyone, behave yourselves!

182
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:14,110
Mom, for the teacher, not tea,

183
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:16,200
serve coffee. Coffee, I said.

184
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:18,300
Excuse me.

185
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:19,540
She's here.

186
00:12:22,300 --> 00:12:25,508
Yoko-sensei, welcome, welcome!

187
00:12:25,558 --> 00:12:27,960
That wasn't a pun.

188
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:30,760
Teacher, this is my mom.

189
00:12:30,810 --> 00:12:32,897
And this is my little brother, Kinjiro.

190
00:12:32,947 --> 00:12:35,560
And this is my dad.

191
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:40,140
That's Dad's Osaka thing, isn't it!

192
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:43,660
Yeah, Teacher. Let's go now.

193
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:44,760
I'll visit again.

194
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:49,380
But you know, partings have
a way of coming out of nowhere.

195
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:52,080
Teacher, you're quitting?

196
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:55,700
Kuruma-sensei has finished
recuperating at home

197
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:58,260
and will be back at school next week.

198
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:01,080
So I'll be saying goodbye to everyone soon.

199
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:02,020
No way.

200
00:13:02,020 --> 00:13:02,940
Shit.

201
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:05,920
Ramming Kuruma-sensei with a bicycle

202
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,000
Maybe I'll get him hospitalized again.

203
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:11,080
Even as a joke,
you shouldn't say things like that.

204
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:11,860
But...

205
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:13,820
Even when I go back to university,

206
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:15,900
I won't forget you,
Kankichi, or everyone else.

207
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:17,740
These three weeks

208
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:20,240
were a precious experience for me too,

209
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:24,900
and I really felt I'd never
become a proper member of society.

210
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:31,520
Don't look so down.
That's not like you, Ryotsu.

211
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:36,800
I know! Shall we go out somewhere tomorrow,
on Sunday?

212
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:41,340
I never thanked you for
fixing my bicycle chain.

213
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:43,700
Let's go see a movie, Ryotsu.

214
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:44,180
A movie?

215
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:46,380
What kind of movies do you like, Ryotsu?

216
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:49,240
Um... I guess samurai sword-fight movies.

217
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:51,500
Then it's a date, then.

218
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:52,600
It's settled.

219
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:54,540
The time is 10 a.m.

220
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:55,100
Really?

221
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:57,240
Promise, okay?

222
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:59,220
Yeah, it's a promise!

223
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:02,000
Yay!

224
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,820
A movie alone with Teacher Yoko

225
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:06,460
W-wait, this is...

226
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:09,380
It's kind of like a... d-date, I guess!

227
00:14:09,380 --> 00:14:11,560
Yay!

228
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:13,860
Big brother, keep it down!

229
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:15,000
Idiot!

230
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,560
Who could possibly stay quiet?

231
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:18,720
Yeah!

232
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:27,200
The teacher's late

233
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:30,020
The first showing's about to start!

234
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:32,740
I wonder what's wrong.

235
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:39,680
Yes, this is the general store.

236
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:43,060
Oh my, if it isn't Teacher Yoko!

237
00:14:43,060 --> 00:14:44,500
What's the matter?

238
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:45,340
I'm sorry.

239
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:49,700
I had promised to go see a
movie with Kankichi at 10 today,

240
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:52,320
but my aunt suddenly fell ill.

241
00:14:53,940 --> 00:14:56,420
Yes, I'll have to look
after her all day today.

242
00:14:57,180 --> 00:14:59,020
Oh my, that's terrible.

243
00:14:59,620 --> 00:15:02,620
Understood. I'll send word right away.

244
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:06,900
Please. Tell Motokichi-kun I'm truly sorry.

245
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:10,380
Don't be silly.
You don't need to worry about that.

246
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,900
Kinjirō, run over to Oden-on and tell them.

247
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:15,020
Okay!

248
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:30,200
Liar, Teacher!

249
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,840
I'm sorry, Kankichi.

250
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:35,480
But I really couldn't go yesterday.

251
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:38,500
That's selfish. You promised.

252
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:41,300
I hate you, Teacher!

253
00:15:45,140 --> 00:15:49,180
Kankitsu-ya, time is infinite.

254
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,000
You shouldn't think like that.

255
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:55,120
Life has limits.

256
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:58,860
In a life this short,

257
00:15:58,860 --> 00:16:02,900
if you keep listening
to everything others say,

258
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:10,780
today is goodbye to Teacher Yoko Saeki.

259
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:14,220
Thank you for your hard work
during these three short weeks.

260
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:20,420
What about Kankitsu?

261
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:23,840
Kankitsu left right after class ended.

262
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:26,680
What a worthless guy.

263
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:28,900
Kankitsu...

264
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:40,820
Who cares about the teacher?

265
00:16:43,820 --> 00:16:45,160
I hate her, I hate her!

266
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:48,180
Kankichi!

267
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:53,360
Yoko-sensei asked me to
give this to Kankichi.

268
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:00,600
Yoko-sensei?

269
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:10,660
I told you, she's already gone.

270
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:13,400
Sensei looked so lonely, Kankichi.

271
00:17:19,840 --> 00:17:21,620
What are you doing, Kankichi?

272
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:24,940
Take all the curtains down!
We can still make it.

273
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:34,000
You're sure the time she's
taking the train is right?

274
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:37,360
We know which train she's on, so it's fine.

275
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:38,540
Right, hurry!

276
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:48,840
Up close, it's huge.

277
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,700
I had no idea it was this big.

278
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:52,400
What should we do, Kankichi?

279
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:55,340
Once a man makes up his mind,
he'll see it through.

280
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:04,120
Be careful.
If we get caught, we're in big trouble.

281
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:05,260
I know.

282
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:09,860
Whaaaat?

283
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:15,820
What? Oh no, look, they're coming in!

284
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:19,660
Donpei, you get it? Still feels like...

285
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:23,700
Ugh! Gandhi, leave this to me, go!

286
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:25,160
...was doing it.

287
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:26,760
Whaaaat?

288
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:27,260
Hey, wait!

289
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:34,420
Brat!

290
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:37,300
Yeah! Over here, over here!

291
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:40,560
Hey! Wait up!

292
00:18:54,660 --> 00:18:55,760
This wind is insane!

293
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:58,740
This is unexpected!

294
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:03,060
This is unexpected too!

295
00:19:03,060 --> 00:19:04,360
Get out of the way!

296
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:08,720
I can't go!

297
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:12,260
What?

298
00:19:12,740 --> 00:19:13,840
It's the chimney next door!

299
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:18,060
From here, you can only see the
chimney on the Sumida River side!

300
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,660
With that chimney,
it's hidden behind the other one!

301
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:23,360
You idiot! Why didn't you say that sooner!

302
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:25,880
They've gone!

303
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:50,000
Damn it! The train's coming already!
What am I supposed to do?!

304
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:56,680
Alright! If I catch the wind just right,
I might make it!

305
00:19:58,180 --> 00:19:59,020
Hup!

306
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:02,920
Yes! I caught it!

307
00:20:03,460 --> 00:20:06,000
Kankichi!
He's going to jump over to the other side!

308
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:06,800
What?!

309
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,620
Be careful, Kankichi!

310
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:10,120
Okay! Here I go!

311
00:20:10,560 --> 00:20:11,000
Here goes!

312
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:18,960
But it worked!

313
00:20:19,180 --> 00:20:20,760
Hurry up and climb to the top

314
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:22,000
Nice, Kankichi!

315
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:23,160
Do your best!

316
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,940
Reach Yoko-sensei!

317
00:20:31,260 --> 00:20:34,720
Mom, there's something
hanging from the Ghost Chimneys

318
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:36,480
The Ghost Chimneys?

319
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:47,400
Whoa, this is heavy!

320
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:52,600
Thank you, Yoko-sensei.

321
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:55,960
And I'm sorry.

322
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:59,340
That girl, honestly...

323
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:02,660
Thank you, Kankichi-kun.

324
00:21:03,460 --> 00:21:05,760
I'm going to be a good teacher.

325
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:08,420
Goodbye, Kankichi-kun.

326
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:11,660
Did you see that, Sensei?

327
00:21:12,820 --> 00:21:16,180
Gakiji, that was the best!

328
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:19,160
You idiot!

329
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:21,800
I'll turn you all over to the cops,
starting with whoever's first.

330
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:22,580
Got it?

331
00:21:24,940 --> 00:21:27,620
Then we got scolded by the police,

332
00:21:27,620 --> 00:21:29,040
scolded at school,

333
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:30,800
and scolded by our parents.

334
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:32,880
We got scolded a whole lifetime's worth.

335
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:37,200
The last time I climbed
a chimney was back then.

336
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:40,540
And that's the end of my story.

337
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:43,460
Well, I'm getting down now.

338
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:47,980
Ryo-san

339
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:48,860
Junpei

340
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:52,960
Junpei, Mom's coming now, okay?

341
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:57,000
Ma'am, it's dangerous. Leave this to Ryotsu.

342
00:21:57,540 --> 00:21:59,040
But he's my child!

343
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:00,120
Mom

344
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:02,600
Looks like you dropped
everything and came running.

345
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:04,540
Ryo-san

346
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:07,500
Don't worry, I'm not going to get angry.

347
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:08,920
She's your mom, after all.

348
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:10,660
Yeah.

349
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:13,860
Sorry, Mom.

350
00:22:14,350 --> 00:22:15,360
I'll come down right away.

351
00:22:15,830 --> 00:22:16,400
Chunpei!

352
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:17,920
Okay, Chunpei.

353
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:18,960
Follow me down the bridge.

354
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:21,460
Coming down is harder than climbing up,
you know.

355
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:22,340
Yeah.

356
00:22:23,340 --> 00:22:24,300
He's coming down!

357
00:22:24,300 --> 00:22:25,840
Ryo-tsu, you've done it!

358
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:26,740
Big brother.

359
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:34,160
Come on, jump into Mom's arms!

360
00:22:34,540 --> 00:22:37,020
I'm sure she'll hold you tenderly.

361
00:22:38,520 --> 00:22:39,000
Yeah.

362
00:22:40,920 --> 00:22:41,880
Mom...

363
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:44,040
Ready.

364
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:47,660
Mom...

365
00:22:49,320 --> 00:22:49,800
Ready.

366
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:55,220
What a moving moment

367
00:22:56,860 --> 00:22:57,820
Mom...

368
00:22:59,140 --> 00:23:00,680
This time, you idiot son...

369
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:04,800
how can you keep causing
trouble for other people?

370
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,940
I always tell you, don't I?

371
00:23:06,900 --> 00:23:08,080
I'm sorry.

372
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:10,200
Mom...

373
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:13,720
Well, reality's like this.

374
00:23:27,260 --> 00:23:28,900
The Ghost Chimneys

375
00:23:33,660 --> 00:23:38,720
In 1964, even Japan's largest
power plant had become obsolete,

376
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:41,260
and it was finally going to be torn down.

377
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:44,580
That huge,
valiant figure visible from the old downtown

378
00:23:44,580 --> 00:23:47,460
would never be seen again.

379
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:55,280
For us, it felt like one of
our memories was crumbling away.

380
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:57,500
That's how it felt.

381
00:24:05,940 --> 00:24:10,560
Whoa, why am I stuck in this
locker with a naked Honda?

382
00:24:10,560 --> 00:24:14,360
Rugby club members from Muscle-Style who want to be bullied by kids,
and female pro wrestlers,

383
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:16,580
I have to be chased around by them.

384
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:18,020
This is absurd.

385
00:24:18,840 --> 00:24:21,500
Next time,
The Terrifying White Man, see you!

386
00:24:35,780 --> 00:24:44,060
Surprise and commotion, solved at
the right moment, quick to lend a hand,

387
00:24:44,060 --> 00:24:55,700
decided in a flash, bouncing and gathering together,
actions soaring away.

388
00:24:56,740 --> 00:25:00,440
Above all, incredible power.

389
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:06,460
Gather everyone, come here,

390
00:25:07,300 --> 00:25:12,660
like a dream, the final energy.

391
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,140
Gaze at tomorrow, believe in yesterday,

392
00:25:17,140 --> 00:25:20,020
paint the universe, and stand on the ground.

393
00:25:20,020 --> 00:25:23,840
The star of Kameari spun
around and drew a ring.

394
00:25:26,300 --> 00:25:27,400
This'll do, right!

395
00:25:27,680 --> 00:25:28,940
Like hell it will!

